### What each command does: one short sentence under the command palette's list for the
### selected command, and the description screen readers announce for its row. The id is
### the command's own message id followed by "-help".

## Images and zoom

palette-next-help = Go to the next image in the folder.
palette-prev-help = Go to the previous image in the folder.
palette-first-help = Go to the first image in the folder.
palette-last-help = Go to the last image in the folder.
palette-go-to-help = Jump to an image by its number in the folder.
palette-zoom-in-help = Magnify the image one step.
palette-zoom-out-help = Shrink the image one step.
palette-zoom-fit-help = Show the whole image in the window.
palette-zoom-fill-help = Fill the window with the image, cropping its edges if needed.
palette-zoom-fit-width-help = Fit the image's width to the window. In a book, every page then opens this way.
palette-zoom-fit-height-help = Fit the image's height to the window. In a book, every page then opens this way.
palette-zoom-100-help = Show the image at its actual size, one image pixel per screen pixel.
palette-zoom-200-help = Show the image at twice its actual size.
palette-zoom-300-help = Show the image at three times its actual size.
palette-zoom-400-help = Show the image at four times its actual size.
palette-zoom-rectangle-help = Drag a rectangle over the image to zoom into it.
palette-rotate-left-help = Turn the image a quarter turn to the left. The file is not changed.
palette-rotate-right-help = Turn the image a quarter turn to the right. The file is not changed.
palette-flip-horizontal-help = Mirror the image left to right. The file is not changed.
palette-flip-vertical-help = Mirror the image top to bottom. The file is not changed.

## Inspecting

